        "title": "Area Rule",
        "text": "The area of a triangle when two sides and the included angle are known is:\\n\\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$$\\n\\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the two sides and $C$ is the angle between them.",
